Conversio: use a transparent NSCursor for Windows hidden-cursor requests.

Based on the cursor-only approach proposed by Elvin Hayatov in Wine MR 11880
(and MR 11799 v4 1/4); no GCMouse/raw-input changes are included.
https://gitlab.winehq.org/wine/wine/-/merge_requests/11880

On macOS 26 GTA5.exe can remain active, with ShowCursor count negative and
clientWantsCursorHidden=cursorHidden=TRUE, while CGCursorIsVisible returns TRUE.
Avoid the hide/unhide counter and reassert the empty cursor after AppKit resets.
Cursor Location Assistance is disabled only for the Wine app, not system-wide.
Visible Windows cursors, pointer exit and animated cursor requests are retained.

--- a/dlls/winemac.drv/cocoa_app.m
+++ b/dlls/winemac.drv/cocoa_app.m
@@ -86,6 +86,22 @@
 }

 
+/* A hidden cursor can be made visible by macOS Cursor Location Assistance.
+ * Keep the cursor plane visible with an empty image instead (Wine MR 11880,
+ * Elvin Hayatov). Do not accumulate NSCursor hide/unhide counts. */
+static NSCursor* transparent_cursor(void)
+{
+    static NSCursor* cursor;
+    static dispatch_once_t once;
+
+    dispatch_once(&once, ^{
+        NSImage* image = [[NSImage alloc] initWithSize:NSMakeSize(1, 1)];
+        cursor = [[NSCursor alloc] initWithImage:image hotSpot:NSZeroPoint];
+        [image release];
+    });
+    return cursor;
+}
+
